      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "09a7bbba_ab4628df",
        "filename": "driver/ioexpander/it8801.c",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 284,
      "author": {
        "id": 1113904
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-01-10T20:36:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we\u0027re at this line, inside a low priority task, and another higher priority task interrupts us and sets another gpio on the same port, when we resume this task, we\u0027ll have an old \"val\" thus clobbering the higher priority task\u0027s gpio change.\n\nThe way it is now (not considering caching either), I think this needs at least some per port locking.",
      "revId": "ab90e041e67e3a47bec2c5d7a88d1932f2777591",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
